From 7daf5578260e6c6270d447ec9edb3a1bb001edf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Markus Volk <f_l_k@t-online.de>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:51:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] DRM: software rendering: keep the kernel's mode, flip
 persistent buffers

With GRAPHICS_API_OPENGL_SOFTWARE the first mode of the connector was
used, whatever size the application asked for. On a TV listing eight
1920x1080 modes, booted with video=1920x1080@60, this picked a mode with
other timings than the one the kernel had set, and the TV showed the
picture shifted, a part of the left edge at the right.

Select the mode like the hardware path does, and prefer the mode the
CRTC shows already when it has the requested size and refresh rate. The
comparison is done on the timings, as FindMatchingConnectorMode() only
compares the first bytes of the modes.

Every frame also created a new dumb buffer, which the kernel clears,
and did a full mode set with it. Create two dumb buffers once, keep them
mapped and show each frame with a page flip.

Upstream-Status: Pending
